  "decision_conditions": [
    "The development hereby permitted shall be commenced before the expiration of three years from the date of this permission.<br>",
    "<p>The development hereby approved shall only be carried out in accordance with the following approved plans and documents:</p><ul><li>Site Location Plan&nbsp;&nbsp;(received: 12/12/2024)</li><li>Design and Access Statement (received: 12/12/2024)</li><li>Proposed Site Plan (drawing no: ZAAVIA/29FR/313,&nbsp; issue: A, dated: 05/12/2024)</li><li>Existing and Proposed Section Plans (drawing no: ZAAVIA/29FR/311,&nbsp; issue: A, dated: 05/12/2024)</li><li>Proposed Elevations (drawing no: ZAAVIA/29FR/309,&nbsp; issue: A, dated: 05/12/2024)</li><li>Proposed Loft Plan (drawing no: ZAAVIA/29FR/307,&nbsp; issue: A, dated: 05/12/2024)</li><li>Proposed First Floor Plans&nbsp;(drawing no: ZAAVIA/29FR/306,&nbsp; issue: A, dated: 05/12/2024)</li><li>Proposed Ground Floor Plans (drawing no: ZAAVIA/29FR/304,&nbsp; issue: A, dated: 05/12/2024)</li><li>Proposed Site Plan (drawing no: ZAAVIA/29FR/305,&nbsp; issue: A, dated: 05/12/2024)</li><li>FRA and SUDs Assessment&nbsp;(received: 12/12/2024)</li></ul><p>No other drawings or documents apply.</p>",
    "a)&nbsp;Prior to occupation of the proposed flats, details of all cycle storage including the design, quantum and location\r\nshall be submitted to and approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority.\r\nAll cycle storage shall be designed in accordance with the London Cycle Design\r\nStandards. b)&nbsp;The approved cycle storage shall be implemented and thereafter\r\nmaintained for the lifetime of the development. ",
    "No works above foundation level shall take place until the applicant has entered into an agreement for off-site highways works with the Council for the removal of the crossover and the restoration of the kerb outside the property. Confirmation of the off-site highways agreement shall be submitted to and approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority prior to any works above foundation level.&nbsp;"
  ],
